  "articleBody": "Building garage walls that aren't perfectly square can cause a cascade of problems down the line, and it's a more common mistake than you might think. When your walls aren't square, it makes everything that comes next a real struggle. Think about trying to install drywall—it won't sit flush, creating gaps and uneven surfaces. Then there's the issue of hanging shelves or cabinets; they'll look crooked and could even be unstable. Even worse, if you're trying to add a garage door, an out-of-square opening means the door won't fit right, leading to operational issues, air leaks, and a less secure garage. It's really tough to fix these issues once the walls are up and secured, so getting it right from the start is super important. That's why folks who know their stuff always emphasize checking for square and plumb at every stage of framing. If you're tackling a garage framing project and want to avoid these headaches, or if you're already in a pickle with crooked walls, calling in a seasoned pro from HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of grief. They can ensure your framing is spot-on from the get-go.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}